  "posted_text": "🔑 Housing\nPA HB 2023 — Landlord Can Delay Eviction in Extreme Weather\n\nPennsylvania courts could temporarily pause eviction notices if extreme weather conditions – like freezing temperatures, winter storms, hurricanes, or excessive heat – threaten a tenant’s property. This would give the landlord and tenant up to five days to complete the eviction once the weather improves. ...\n...",
